XII. SECRETARY — CONTINUITY AND ORCHESTRATION SERVICE

Definition

The Secretary is your proposed always-on administrative and system-orchestration service.

Its primary purpose is to detect continuity problems, evaluate system events, and route authorized notifications or administrative actions.

It acts as an intermediary between system components.

Principal responsibilities

1. Monitor authorized system health signals.
2. Detect missing or inconsistent records.
3. Identify continuity interruptions.
4. Check relevant account and device references.
5. Evaluate authorization conditions.
6. Route events to the appropriate subsystem.
7. Generate alerts.
8. Preserve event history.
9. Synchronize approved profile information.
10. Support authorized administrative workflows.

A-to-A continuity

Your A-to-A terminology can be provisionally interpreted as an account-to-account or application-to-application continuity relationship.

The precise meaning needs to be established in the Codex.

A continuity event might occur when:

- A registered device stops reporting.
- A required record is missing.
- A timestamp is inconsistent.
- A verification process fails.
- An account credential expires.
- A data transfer is incomplete.
- A system service becomes unavailable.

Proposed Secretary workflow

flowchart TD
    A["System event detected"] --> B["Identify source account and device"]
    B --> C["Check authorization"]
    C --> D{"Authorized event?"}
    D -->|No| E["Reject or quarantine"]
    D -->|Yes| F["Classify event"]
    F --> G["Check continuity and data integrity"]
    G --> H{"Verification passed?"}
    H -->|No| I["Generate exception alert"]
    H -->|Yes| J["Route to authorized subsystem"]
    I --> K["Preserve event record"]
    J --> K
    K --> L["Human review when required"]
    L --> M["Record outcome and provenance"]

The Secretary should not silently alter source evidence or independently authorize sensitive surveillance activities.

Its authority should be limited by a defined permission model.

BST — Buy, Sell, Trade

BST can be integrated as an account-based commercial or administrative service.

Potential functions:

- Asset registration.
- Resource availability.
- Purchase orders.
- Sales records.
- Trade documentation.
- Invoices.
- Account balances.
- Settlement records.

However, financial transactions should remain separate from evidence verification.

An invoice cannot establish the truth of an observation.

A token transaction cannot establish the legitimacy of a drone mission.

Secretary and 3E

Your architecture has two previously defined interpretations of 3E:

Version	Components	Application

3E v1	Evidence • Ethics • Epistemics	Information governance
3E v2	Economic • Ecological • Environmental	Resource and environmental evaluation


Both can be incorporated as separate evaluation frameworks.

They should not be collapsed into a single undefined 3E variable.


