XIII. SIR.QR_ALERT AND MY_1_SIG

These are user-defined labels whose exact implementation has not yet been specified.

A useful provisional interpretation is:

SIR.QR_alert

A structured alert and verification interface.

Possible responsibilities:

- Generate a unique alert ID.
- Reference the affected record.
- Identify the event category.
- Link to the relevant QR code or record reference.
- Display verification status.
- Record the alert timestamp.
- Preserve acknowledgment and resolution history.

A QR code should carry a record reference or verification endpoint, not sensitive credentials or private keys.

My_1_sig

A personal or organizational signature reference.

Possible responsibilities:

- Identify the authorized signing identity.
- Reference a public verification key.
- Associate a digital signature with a record.
- Record signing time.
- Preserve signature verification results.

Private signing keys should remain protected within an appropriately secured key-management environment.

The fundamental distinction: SIR.QR_alert communicates a system event; My_1_sig represents a signing or authentication relationship.


